---
description: Rules for the SketchUp bridge (Ruby) and MCP server
globs: extensions/**, python/df_geometry/**
---

- SketchUp Ruby API runs on the main thread only. Never use `Thread.new` for model access; poll from `UI.start_timer`.
- Every batch of model changes is wrapped in `model.start_operation(name, true)` / `commit_operation`, with `abort_operation` on error.
- Convert mm → inches with `.mm` and back with `.to_mm` at the boundary. Wire format is always mm.
- Never trigger UI that can open a modal dialog (`Sketchup.file_new` on a modified model, `UI.messagebox`, export option dialogs with `show_summary: true`).
- New bridge ops must be added to the `OPS` whitelist in Ruby AND as a Pydantic command in `df_geometry/commands.py`, with a compiler test.
- File paths must go through `safe_path` (job root only).
- `eval_ruby` is debug-only (`DF_ALLOW_EVAL=1`); production builds must not register it.
- Bump `VERSION` in the bridge on any behaviour change; geometry cache keys include it.
